            <ArticleTitle>Perception of triggers in young nonclinical school students with migrainous headaches and with tension headaches.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>284-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In an exploratory study of a general population of 209 young children (M = 12.9 yr. old), 59% of those with migraine or tension headache (n = 41) reported one or more triggers. More triggers were reported from those with tension headaches than from those with migrainous headaches.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
